From a9e176c2baeb0ed00b2d08491e351dba33a8318f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Brunner <michael.brunner@sm0x.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:12:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] image: initialise FpImage.ppmm

FpImage.ppmm is documented as the image resolution and is handed to
get_minutiae(), but nothing ever assigns it.  FpImage has only "width"
and "height" properties and fp_image_init() is empty, so the field is
always the zero left by GObject's allocation.

Inside NBIS the value reaches combined_minutia_quality(), which derives
the neighbourhood radius from it:

    radius_pix = sround(RADIUS_MM * ppmm);

With ppmm zero the radius is zero, so grayscale_reliability() computes
the mean and standard deviation of an empty neighbourhood for every
minutia.  The resulting reliability is meaningless.

Today that is invisible: minutiae_to_xyt() stores the reliability in
c[i].col[3] and then copies only col[0..2] into the xyt structure, so it
never reaches Bozorth.  The XXX comment right above that function
suggests selecting the highest quality minutiae instead of the first
MAX_BOZORTH_MINUTIAE - an improvement that would silently build on
garbage while ppmm stays zero.

Initialise it to the 500 dpi the NBIS parameters are tuned for and that
the existing documentation already assumed, and note that drivers may
override it.  No matching behaviour changes.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libfprint/fp-image.c  | 12 ++++++++++--
 libfprint/fpi-image.h |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/fp-image.c b/libfprint/fp-image.c
index f9c60b3..be8d69e 100644
--- a/libfprint/fp-image.c
+++ b/libfprint/fp-image.c
@@ -153,9 +153,16 @@ fp_image_class_init (FpImageClass *klass)
   g_object_class_install_properties (object_class, N_PROPS, properties);
 }
 
+/* NBIS derives pixel distances from the scan resolution.  Drivers that know
+ * their sensor's real resolution should override FpImage.ppmm; everything
+ * else is assumed to be the 500 dpi that the NBIS parameters are tuned for.
+ */
+#define FP_IMAGE_DEFAULT_PPMM (500.0 / 25.4)
+
 static void
 fp_image_init (FpImage *self)
 {
+  self->ppmm = FP_IMAGE_DEFAULT_PPMM;
 }
 
 typedef struct
@@ -382,8 +389,9 @@ fp_image_get_width (FpImage *self)
  * fp_image_get_ppmm:
  * @self: A #FpImage
  *
- * Gets the resolution of the image. Note that this is assumed to
- * be fixed to 500 points per inch (~19.685 p/mm) for most drivers.
+ * Gets the resolution of the image. This defaults to 500 points per inch
+ * (~19.685 p/mm), which is the resolution the NBIS parameters are tuned
+ * for; drivers may override it for sensors with a known resolution.
  *
  * Returns: the resolution of the image in points per millimeter
  */
diff --git a/libfprint/fpi-image.h b/libfprint/fpi-image.h
index fdc376c..46ab4c0 100644
--- a/libfprint/fpi-image.h
+++ b/libfprint/fpi-image.h
@@ -45,7 +45,8 @@ typedef enum {
  * FpImage:
  * @width: Width of the image
  * @height: Height of the image
- * @ppmm: Pixels per millimeter
+ * @ppmm: Pixels per millimeter of the sensor. Defaults to 500 dpi;
+ *   drivers should set this when the real resolution is known.
  * @flags: #FpiImageFlags for required normalization
  *
  * Structure holding an image. The public fields are only public for internal
-- 
